### Day capacity setting (K-0024): how many minutes of planned work fit in a weekday and in a weekend day.
### Fill the seed account values from user-secrets: Seed:SahipEmail / Seed:SahipPassword
### (and Seed:AsistanEmail / Seed:AsistanPassword for the 403 example). Do not commit real values.

@host = http://localhost:5051
@sahipEmail = <Seed:SahipEmail>
@sahipSifre = <Seed:SahipPassword>
@asistanEmail = <Seed:AsistanEmail>
@asistanSifre = <Seed:AsistanPassword>

### 1. Log in as Sahip
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/hesap/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{sahipEmail}}", "password": "{{sahipSifre}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. Read it (takvim.oku): without a saved value it is `Gun:KapasiteSaat` for both kinds of day
GET {{host}}/api/ayarlar/gun
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Set it (the Sahip only): 4 hours on weekdays, 2 on weekends -> 200
PUT {{host}}/api/ayarlar/gun
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "haftaIciDk": 240, "haftaSonuDk": 120 }

### 3b. Refused: out of 1..1440 -> 400 { errors: { haftaIciDk } }
PUT {{host}}/api/ayarlar/gun
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "haftaIciDk": 0, "haftaSonuDk": 120 }

### 4. The Asistan may read it, not change it -> 403
# @name asistanLogin
POST {{host}}/api/hesap/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{asistanEmail}}", "password": "{{asistanSifre}}" }

###
PUT {{host}}/api/ayarlar/gun
Authorization: Bearer {{asistanLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "haftaIciDk": 240, "haftaSonuDk": 120 }
